## Runtime data flow

1. **`seat_lookup.py`** loads `seats_lookup.json` (union of all seats across all variants) + `seating_variants.json` on first use.
2. The active variant determines which `availability_*.json` is loaded. Every variant has an explicit availability file -- navigation and teleportation are strictly limited to seats present in the active variant's availability set.
3. `get_seat_position()` always returns a position (seat exists in any variant). `is_seat_available()` checks the active availability set.
4. Switching variant via `seatLayoutChange` event: unhighlights any active seat, updates USD VariantSet on the SeatInstancer prim, calls `seat_lookup.set_active_variant()` to swap the availability filter, then invalidates the seat highlight cache.

## Seat prototype override service (seat_proto_override.py)

Single owner of the seat instancer's session-layer `protoIndices` opinion. Three callers (`seat_highlight`, `seat_fold_state`, and the unhighlight nav-visited write) need to flip prototype indices on the same PointInstancer attribute — doing it from each module independently means whichever writes last wins, which would lose fold-state every time a highlight is applied (and vice versa). This module is the only place that writes the override; everyone else routes through `set_one` / `clear_one` / `set_overrides` / `set_down_for_seat`.

Internal state is `{instance_idx: (proto_idx, priority)}`; `_flush()` rebuilds the merged array from the variant baseline + every override and writes it once. The variant baseline is read by walking the property stack and skipping the session layer, so our own override never loops back into the merge.

**Priority ladder** (higher wins):

| Constant | Value | Producer | Lifecycle |
|---|---|---|---|
| `FOLD_PRIORITY` | 1 | `seat_fold_state.refresh()` (crowd density change) | Bulk-cleared on every density flip via `set_overrides({}, clear_priority=FOLD_PRIORITY)` |
| `NAV_VISITED_PRIORITY` | 5 | `seat_highlight.unhighlight_seat()` writes one when a route ends | Persists for the rest of the session — survives crowd flips and seating-variant swaps; only cleared by `reset()` (stage close) |
| `HIGHLIGHT_PRIORITY` | 10 | `seat_highlight.highlight_seat()` writes one for the active nav target | Cleared by `unhighlight_seat()` (then immediately replaced with a NAV_VISITED Down at the same index) |

**Helpers**:

| Function | Use |
|---|---|
| `set_one(idx, proto, prio)` | Single-index override |
| `clear_one(idx, prio)` | Drop one override **only if its priority matches** — guards against highlight clearing fold-state, etc. |
| `set_overrides(updates, clear_priority=None)` | Bulk write at one priority; `clear_priority` drops every existing override at that level first |
| `set_down_for_seat(idx, prio)` | Reads variant baseline at idx (0/1), maps via `_UP_TO_DOWN` to the matching Down (2/3), writes the override. Used by both `seat_fold_state` and `unhighlight_seat`. No-op for indices that don't sit on a known Up prototype. |
| `get_baseline_proto(idx)` | Diagnostic — variant-baseline proto at idx |
| `reapply()` | Re-flush against the current baseline. Called after `seating` variant change so existing overrides survive the baseline swap. |
| `reset()` | Drop everything (e.g. stage close) |

**Seating variant interaction**: `_on_seat_layout_change` in `extension.py` calls `seat_proto_override.reapply()` immediately after the USD VariantSet flips, then `seat_fold_state.refresh()`. Variant order is generator-stable, so visited / fold overrides at instance idx N still target the same seat after the flip.

## Seat highlighting (seat_highlight.py)

Runtime per-seat highlight using PointInstancer prototype swapping. Routes through `seat_proto_override` so highlight composes with crowd-driven Down-state and nav-visited Down-state without clobbering them.

**Key design**: All highlight edits are written to the **session layer** so they never pollute the VariantSet data on the root layer. This prevents corruption when switching variants while a seat is highlighted.

| Function | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `highlight_seat(seat_number)` | Reads `primvars:seatId` to find the instance index, calls `seat_proto_override.set_one(idx, HIGHLIGHT_INDEX=4, HIGHLIGHT_PRIORITY)`. Auto-unhighlights any previously highlighted seat first. |
| `unhighlight_seat()` | Clears the highlight override, then **writes a NAV_VISITED Down override** at the same index via `set_down_for_seat` so the seat stays unfolded — the user has effectively sat down (see "Nav-visited Down state" below). Restores the seated-crowd character. |
| `invalidate_cache()` | Clears the `seatId -> index` mapping (must be called after variant switch since instance arrays change) |
| `get_highlighted_seat()` | Returns the currently highlighted seat number or `None` |

**Seat ID format**: Full IDs like `"A-4-15"` are used directly for lookup (case-insensitive fallback). No zero-padding.

**Instancer path**: `/World/Skandinavium/seats_instanced/SeatInstancer`

### Nav-visited Down state

When a seat route ends — auto-walk arrival, manual stop, proximity arrival, dismiss, switching to a different seat — `unhighlight_seat()` does **not** clear the seat back to baseline. It writes a `NAV_VISITED_PRIORITY` Down override so the chair stays unfolded for the rest of the session. Rationale: the user has "sat down" there, the chair shouldn't fold up behind them.

| Behaviour | Why |
|---|---|
| Survives crowd density flips | Visited (priority 5) > FOLD (priority 1); the bulk-clear in `set_overrides(..., clear_priority=FOLD_PRIORITY)` only touches priority-1 entries. |
| Survives seating-variant flips | `seat_proto_override.reapply()` re-flushes overrides against the new baseline; instance order is variant-stable in the generator so the visited idx still maps to the right seat. |
| Loses to a new highlight | `HIGHLIGHT_PRIORITY` (10) > `NAV_VISITED_PRIORITY` (5); when the highlight is cleared, the visited Down on that seat is rewritten (it's the same priority-5 opinion that was already present, plus a fresh one from the new arrival). |
| Cleared on stage close | `seat_proto_override.reset()` wipes everything; the override map is process-local. |

**Wheelchair / companion seats**: visited Down is a no-op for these. Wheelchair seats live under `/World/WheelchairSpots` (separate Xforms, not in the PointInstancer); companion seats are in the instancer but are not navigable (`is_seat_available` returns False / never gets a `seatNavigate`). For both, no highlight ever writes a HIGHLIGHT override → no `unhighlight_seat()` call → no visited Down. Works as intended.

### Seated-crowd character hide (companion to highlight)

`highlight_seat()` and `unhighlight_seat()` also drive `seated_crowd_highlight.py` so the **sitting character** on the target seat is removed from view while the seat route is active — otherwise the green chair would be mostly occluded by a seated body. The hide rides on the existing seat-highlight lifecycle, so every existing call site (route stop, seat layout switch, seat teleport completion, bird-eye seat-directions teardown, …) restores the character automatically — no per-call-site wiring.

It also re-applies on `seatedCrowdLayoutChanged` (observed by `navmesh_route_extension/extension.py`), so toggling "Display crowd" off/on or switching density via the dev picker mid-route keeps the target uncovered.

The hide is a silent no-op when the seated-crowd payload has not loaded yet, when the seat is wheelchair/companion (no character placed), or when the current `crowd_density` variant already hides that character.

**Mechanism, regen requirement, the `primvars:seatId` lookup, and the session-layer `invisibleIds` union → see `.cursor/rules/topics/seated-crowd.mdc` § "Per-seat character hide".**

## Kit backend (younite.navmesh_route_extension)

### `seat_nav_target_bridge.py`

Small process-wide bridge so **player core** can read the same **seat id** and optional **cached snap `[x,y,z]`** that navigation set when the user requested directions. Populated in `extension.py` when a seat route is calculated (`set_seat_nav_target_seat_id(seat_number, pos)`); cleared on seat stop, seat teleport, and other route teardown paths. Player core uses it in `_on_auto_move_complete` to snap via `TeleportService` (fallback: `get_seat_position` if cache empty) **before** dispatching `autoMoveStatus`, so the celebration runs at the exact seat pose.

### Payload parsing: `_resolve_seat_number(payload)`

Shared helper used by both `_on_seat_navigate` and `_on_seat_teleport`. Builds the seat ID from structured or legacy payloads:

1. If `{ section, row, seat }` fields are all present -> returns `"section-row-seat"` (e.g. `"A-4-15"`)
2. Otherwise falls back to `seatNumber` string (legacy)

### Event: `seatNavigate`
- **Handler**: `_on_seat_navigate` in `extension.py`
- **Payload**: `{ section: string, row: string, seat: string, action?: "navigate"|"stop" }` (or legacy `{ seatNumber: string }`)
- **Navigate flow**: Resolves seat ID via `_resolve_seat_number()`, looks up position via `seat_lookup.get_seat_position()`, checks availability via `is_seat_available()`, highlights the seat via `seat_highlight.highlight_seat()`, then calls `self._svc.set_route_for_id("seat_nav", ..., face_direction=True)`. On the first successful waypoint dispatch, the player's camera instantly turns to face the route direction. Route measure is computed automatically since `routeId != "player"`.
- **Stop flow**: Stops the route, calls `seat_highlight.unhighlight_seat()`.
- **Response event**: `seatNavigateResult` with `{ seatNumber, success, position?, error? }` -- `position` is `[x, y, z]` on success.

### Event: `seatLayoutChange`
- **Handler**: `_on_seat_layout_change` in `extension.py`
- **Payload**: `{ variant: string }` (empty = query current)
- **Flow**: Unhighlights active seat first, sets USD VariantSet `"seating"` on the SeatInstancer prim, calls `seat_lookup.set_active_variant()`, invalidates highlight cache.
- **Response event**: `seatLayoutChanged` with `{ variant, success, variants[] }`.

### Route failure relay: `navmeshRouteError`

When any route calculation fails (the async NavMesh path query returns no result), the internal `navmeshRouteWaypoints` event fires with `success: false`. A listener in `extension.py` relays this as a `navmeshRouteError` outbound event with `{ routeId, error }`. This is generic -- works for `seat_nav`, `exit_nav`, `poi_nav`, `quiet_zone_nav`, and any future route type.

### Key module: `seat_lookup.py`
- `get_seat_position(seat_number) -> tuple | None`
- `is_seat_available(seat_number) -> bool | None`
- `get_seat_positions_bbox_center_xz() -> tuple | None` -- axis-aligned bbox center of all seat positions in **XZ** (cached; cleared on `reload()`). Used as "bowl / stadium plan center" for facing.
- `camera_local_yaw_to_face_world_xz(player_prim, observer_x, observer_z, target_x, target_z) -> float | None` -- camera-local yaw (deg) to look from a world XZ point toward a target XZ point; same convention as `NavigationOrchestratorService.face_toward_world_xz` (`atan2` + player root yaw).
- `get_available_variants() -> dict`
- `set_active_variant(name)` / `get_active_variant()`
- `reload()` -- called on shutdown to reset state (also clears bbox cache).

### Route measurement integration
The `seat_nav` route goes through `set_route_for_id()` which creates a `_RouteInstance`. Since `routeId != "player"`, the route engine (using types and helpers from the `route_measure` package) computes distance and estimated time (base + crowd-adjusted) automatically. The measure is dispatched as `navmeshRouteMeasure` with `routeId: "seat_nav"`.

**Update cadence**: Between full recalcs, lightweight remaining-distance updates use **`LIGHTWEIGHT_MEASURE_INTERVAL_SEC`** from `route_engine/constants.py` (`_periodic_loop` in `route_engine/instance_base.py`; `_emit_lightweight_measure` in `route_engine/arrival.py` — project player onto stored polyline; no NavMesh re-query). During auto-move, full recalcs are suppressed -- only lightweight measures fire. When auto-move stops, a full recalc runs immediately. See `.cursor/rules/topics/route-measurement.mdc`.

**Arrival logic (`_emit_lightweight_measure`)** -- seat-specific:

| Mode | When Kit stops / notifies |
|------|---------------------------|
| **Auto-move on** | Under **1 m** along polyline (`ROUTE_ARRIVAL_THRESHOLD_CM`): route **stays active** (log once); completion is polyline end (or **AABB** on final approach via `PointClickAutoMover`) -> `stop(arrived)` -> player core seat snap -> `autoMoveStatus` -> web celebration. |
| **Auto-move off** | Player inside **seat-manual endpoint AABB** (wider XZ than generic POI) **and** remaining along path ≤ `ARRIVAL_PATH_GUARD_MAX_REMAINING_CM`: `navmeshRouteArrival` with **`manualNearDestination: true`**, `stop(waypoint_error="lightweight_arrival")` -- web runs the **same** celebration as auto-walk but passes **`skipFaceTowardCenter`** so the user is not rotated toward bowl center after free walk. |

Other POIs use the **generic** endpoint AABB half-extents and the same path guard.

**Arrival volume**: World-axis-aligned box centered on the **last polyline vertex**, rebuilt when the path updates (`route_engine/instance_base.py`, dimensions from `route_engine/constants.py`). See `.cursor/rules/topics/route-measurement.mdc` § lightweight updates.

## Web frontend (SeatNavigateWidget + StreamOnlyWindow.tsx + UIControls.tsx)

### SeatNavigateWidget

**File**: `widgets/SeatNavigateWidget.tsx`

The widget presents three cascading dropdowns (CU mode) — **Section**, **Row**, **Seat** — for **both** walking and wheelchair mesh modes. Wheelchair uses the same cascade and `SeatQuery` shape as walking (uppercase `section`/`row`, numeric `seat`; canonical ids like **`G-6-3`**). See "Structured seat input (SeatQuery)" above; the dev panel keeps free-text inputs for all three fields.

Two action buttons (both disabled until all fields are filled):
- **Get directions** -- calculates a NavMesh route (`seatNavigate` event)
- **Teleport me there** -- instant teleport (`seatTeleport` event, see `poi-teleport.mdc`)

The widget also shows:
- Cost toggles: "Avoid crowds" / "Avoid noise"
- Route measure (distance + time) when a route is active
- "Move to seat" auto-walk button when a route is active
- Error messages for not-found, not-available, and unreachable seats

**Props**:
```typescript
onSeatNavigate: (query: SeatQuery) => void;
onSeatTeleport?: (query: SeatQuery) => void;
accessibilityMode: 'wheelchair' | 'walking';
activeSeatRouteId: string | null;
movingToSeatId: string | null;
onSeatMoveStart: () => void;
onSeatMoveStop: () => void;
```

### State variables
| Variable | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `activeSeatRouteId` | `string \| null` | Seat ID with active route, or `"not_found:X"` / `"not_available:X"` / `"unreachable:X"` for errors |
| `movingToSeatId` | `string \| null` | Seat ID the player is auto-moving toward (null = not moving) |
| `lastSeatPositionRef` | `ref<number[]>` | Cached `[x,y,z]` from last successful `seatNavigateResult` -- needed for auto-move |
| `seatingLayout` | `string \| null` | Currently active seating layout variant name |
| `availableSeatingLayouts` | `string[]` | All variant names available for switching (populated from `seatLayoutChanged` response) |
| `seatArrivalLabel` | `string \| null` | Seat key captured on arrival (before `activeSeatRouteId` is cleared). Drives the arrival overlay card during the 5 s celebration. Auto-cleared when celebration ends. |

### Error states

| `activeSeatRouteId` prefix | Meaning | Display |
|---|---|---|
| `not_found:` | Seat ID not in lookup | "Seat X does not exist" |
| `not_available:` | Seat exists but not in current variant | "Seat X is not available" |
| `unreachable:` | Seat found but NavMesh path failed | "Seat X is unreachable -- no walkable path found" |

Errors auto-clear after 3-5 seconds. While an error prefix is present, `hasValidRoute` is false and the Move/Stop buttons are hidden.

### Variant query timing
The available seating layouts are queried from Kit at two points:
1. **Stream start** (`handleStreamStarted`): sends `seatLayoutChange` with empty variant
2. **Scene loaded** (`scene.loaded` event): re-queries to handle cases where Kit wasn't ready at stream start

### Seat route flow
1. User fills in Section, Row, and Seat -> clicks "Get directions".
2. `handleSeatNavigate(query)` sets `activeSeatRouteId = seatKey`, calls `markRouteCalculating('seat_nav')` to **close the ready gate**, then sends `seatNavigate` with `{ section, row, seat }` to Kit. The seat panel stays visible (button label flips to "Stop") because `seatStreamOverlayActive` is gated on `routeReadyByRouteId['seat_nav']`.
3. Kit resolves the seat ID, highlights the seat, dispatches `seatNavigateResult { success: true, position }` (position saved to `lastSeatPositionRef`), then computes the route (`face_direction=True`).
4. When pathfinding completes, Kit's `navmesh_route_extension` relays a **`navmeshRouteReady { routeId: 'seat_nav' }`** ping to web. The handler calls `markRouteReady('seat_nav', true)` → `seatStreamOverlayActive` flips true → the seat panel auto-collapses → the **stream overlay + play FAB appear**. Without this gate the FAB would appear immediately on click and silently no-op (because `lastSeatPositionRef` was still empty) — see "Route ready gating" in `bird-eye-route.mdc` for the full rationale.
5. On the first successful waypoint dispatch (`faceDirection: true`), the player's camera **smoothly rotates** to face the route direction (`_face_route_direction` → `_start_face_turn(profile="route")`, **`FACE_ROUTE_*`**: 132°/s peak with `ease_scale_remaining`, look-ahead **800** stage units). Auto-mover yaw is deferred until the turn finishes (`is_face_turn_active`). Periodic recalculations do not trigger this — only the initial calculation after clicking the button.
6. Route is drawn on screen. Route measure (distance + time) is displayed in the widget and below the floating move button.
7. If the NavMesh path query fails, `navmeshRouteError` is received -> `activeSeatRouteId` set to `unreachable:X` and `markRouteReady('seat_nav', false)` keeps the overlay/FAB hidden. The user stays in first-person — we do **not** roll back to bird-eye on failure (there's nowhere good to roll back to and the inline error in the seat panel is enough surface area).

### Auto-move flow (mirrors spot auto-move)
1. **Start**: User clicks "Move to seat X" -> `handleSeatMoveStart()` sends `navigationStateSet` with `{ autoMove: true, routeId: 'seat_nav', endPos: [x,y,z] }`. The orchestrator triggers `navmeshRouteCalculate` (with `autoMove: true`) -> waypoints -> `PointClickAutoMover` moves the player. During auto-move, `_auto_move_active` is `true` on the route instance, suppressing full NavMesh re-queries. Lightweight remaining-distance updates use `LIGHTWEIGHT_MEASURE_INTERVAL_SEC`.
2. **Arrival (auto-move)**: Polyline end -> auto-mover `stop(arrived)` (final translate applied before stop so seat snap is not overwritten) -> player core snaps to `seats_lookup` -> `autoMoveStatus` / `navmeshRouteStop` -> web sends `seatNavigate` stop, celebration overlay, `activeSeatRouteId` / `movingToSeatId` cleared.
3. **Arrival (manual, auto-move off)**: User walks along the drawn route; when remaining polyline distance drops below **2.5 m**, Kit fires `navmeshRouteArrival` with **`manualNearDestination: true`** -> web same celebration as (2) with **`skipFaceTowardCenter: true`** (no arena yaw). Not the old 1 m seat threshold.
4. **Cancelled**: Kit sends `autoMoveStatus { routeId: 'seat_nav', reason: 'cancelled' }` -> route extension clears `_auto_move_active` and triggers immediate recalc -> web re-requests the seat route (highlight stays active). The route now recalculates every 5 s as the user moves freely.
5. **Interrupted (ground click)**: If the user clicks on the ground during auto-move, the orchestrator's `_ensure_auto_move()` detects the route change from `seat_nav` to `player` and dispatches `autoMoveStatus { routeId: 'seat_nav', reason: 'interrupted' }`. The route extension clears `_auto_move_active` and recalculates; the web re-requests the seat route (highlight stays, route redraws every 5 s, play button shown) but does **not** send `navigationStateSet` back -- the orchestrator already set up the player route for the ground click. The user can press play again to resume auto-move to the seat. This applies to all POI auto-move types (seat, exit, restroom, quiet zone, spots).
6. **Manual stop**: User clicks "Stop moving" -> `handleSeatMoveStop()` disables auto-move, re-requests seat route, restores orchestrator to default `routeId: 'player'`.

### Seat label formatting (`formatSeatLabel`)

The stream navigation overlay and arrival card display human-readable labels via `formatSeatLabel()` in `AppStream.tsx`. It converts the raw seat key into a structured label:

| Key | Output |
|---|---|
| `"O-8-11"` | `"Section O, Row 8, Seat 11"` |
| `"C-6-1"` | `"Section C, Row 6, Seat 1"` (canonical wheelchair / ticket-style after post-process) |
| `"C-WC-R1"` | Legacy keys still render as `"Section C, Seat 1"` (row `WC` omitted; `R`+digits collapsed to the number) for overlays and old bookmarks |

For current data, wheelchair keys match the same **section / row / seat** pattern as walking. The **`WC`** + **`R\d+`** branch in `formatSeatLabel` remains for **legacy** seat strings only.

### Arrival feedback (mode-dependent)

Seat and POI arrival feedback is split by app mode (`appModeRef` on `EventStateSetters`). Kit sends the same events regardless of mode; the frontend event handlers branch:

| Mode | Seat arrival | POI arrival (restroom, quiet zone, POI/geo teleport) |
|---|---|---|
| **CU** | `scheduleSeatArrivalCelebration` — full-screen confetti overlay + arrival card (5 s) | `schedulePoiArrival` — top-bar arrival overlay (5 s) |
| **Dev** | `showTriggerNotification` — compact bottom toast (5 s) | `showTriggerNotification` — compact bottom toast (5 s) |

This prevents CU celebration overlays from appearing in dev mode and dev toasts from appearing in CU mode.

**`appModeRef` wiring**: `StreamOnlyWindow.tsx` creates a `useRef<AppMode>` that mirrors the current `useAppMode().mode` value. The ref is passed into the `useCustomEventHandler` setters object as `appModeRef`. Event handlers read `s.appModeRef.current` synchronously at dispatch time (no stale closures).

#### CU celebration overlay

When in CU mode, a 5-second celebration is shown on seat arrival:

1. **Confetti/throne graphic** -- full-screen `stream-seat-arrival-celebration` PNG (pop animation).
2. **Arrival navigation card** -- the top stream overlay stays visible during celebration with the formatted seat label, speaker/close buttons, and a "You have arrived !" pill (styled like the turn-hint bubble). No metrics or play/pause FAB.
3. **Find my seat panel** (`SeatNavigateWidget`) is auto-closed.

**Data flow**: Arrival handlers (`navigationHandlers.ts`, `seatHandlers.ts`) store the seat key in `seatArrivalLabel` via `setSeatArrivalLabel(prev)` _before_ clearing `activeSeatRouteId`. `StreamOnlyWindow` passes `seatArrivalLabel` and `onArrivalDismiss` to `AppStream`. The label is auto-cleared when `seatArrivalCelebrationVisible` goes false.

**Dismiss**: The X button on the arrival card calls `dismissArrivalCelebration()` which clears both celebration and label immediately, cancelling the 5 s timer.

#### Dev toast

When in dev mode, seat and POI arrivals show a `TriggerZoneToast` (dark pill at bottom center, 5 s auto-dismiss). Rendered via `SharedOverlayLayer` using `ctrl.triggerZoneNotification` state from `ControlContext`.

### Face toward bowl center (walk / auto-move / manual arrival only)

**Not** used for restroom, exit, or quiet-zone arrival -- only **seat** arrival UX.

When the celebration starts, `scheduleSeatArrivalCelebration()` in `hooks/eventHandlers/helpers.ts` sends **`playerFaceStadiumCenter`** unless **`skipFaceTowardCenter: true`**: set for **seat teleport** (Kit already set yaw) and for **manual walk to seat** (`manualNearDestination` from Kit -- user approached from an arbitrary direction).

**Kit bridge** (`navmesh_route_extension/extension.py`): observes `playerFaceStadiumCenter`, reads `get_seat_positions_bbox_center_xz()`, dispatches **`playerFaceWorldXZ`** `{ x, z }`.

**Player core** (`navigation_orchestrator_service.py`): observes `playerFaceWorldXZ`, calls **`face_toward_world_xz`** → `_start_face_turn(profile="stadium")`.

**Stadium profile motion** (tuned for continuous sweep, no rate×ease cruise plateau):

1. `_capture_face_turn_span` stores `start_yaw`, signed `total_delta`, and `duration_s = clamp(|Δ| / FACE_STADIUM_AVG_DEG_PER_S, FACE_STADIUM_DURATION_MIN_S, FACE_STADIUM_DURATION_MAX_S)`.
2. Each `GLOBAL_EVENT_UPDATE` frame: `yaw = start_yaw + total_delta × smootherstep01(elapsed_s / duration_s)` (`ease_helpers.smootherstep01`).
3. Current constants: **`FACE_STADIUM_AVG_DEG_PER_S`** **74**, min duration **0.45 s**, max **1.65 s**, snap within **0.35°**.

Tune stadium speed by lowering/raising **`FACE_STADIUM_AVG_DEG_PER_S`** only (hot-reload). Route-start facing uses a different profile — **`FACE_ROUTE_*`** rate×ease — see `cct-movement.mdc` and `route-measurement.mdc`.

**`stop_face_turn_if_active()`** cancels an in-progress turn when teleport or **`immediateViewAngles`** applies yaw synchronously.

### Seat teleport: view fade + spawn facing (no post-teleport smooth turn)

**Web** (`useSeatNavigation.ts`): `handleSeatTeleport` wraps **`beginViewTransition`** (same pattern as `handlePoiTeleport` in `useNavmeshCore.ts`): fade out -> `onFadeOutComplete` sends `seatTeleport` -> Kit -> `viewTransitionReady` -> fade in.

**Kit** (`_on_seat_teleport`): Computes camera-local yaw toward the seating bbox center via `camera_local_yaw_to_face_world_xz` + `get_seat_positions_bbox_center_xz`. Calls **`TeleportService.teleport_to_coordinates(x, y, z, camera_local_yaw_deg=...)`** when yaw is valid; otherwise position-only. See `.cursor/rules/topics/poi-teleport.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/topics/camera-teleport.mdc`.

**Web** (`seatHandlers.ts`): On successful `seatTeleportResult`, CU mode calls **`scheduleSeatArrivalCelebration(s, { skipFaceTowardCenter: true })`** (no `playerFaceStadiumCenter` -- avoids double-rotation after Kit already set yaw); dev mode calls **`showTriggerNotification`** instead.

### Wheelchair mode auto-revert

When the user navigates in wheelchair mode and reaches the destination (via auto-move, point-and-click, or teleport), the `navmeshMode` is automatically reverted to `'walking'` and a `navmeshModeSet { mode: 'walking' }` message is sent to Kit, triggering a rebake with walking agent settings.

**Revert triggers** (all in `useCustomEventHandler.ts`):
- `autoMoveStatus { reason: 'arrived' }` for `seat_nav`
- `navmeshRouteArrival` for `seat_nav`
- `seatTeleportResult { success: true }`

**Manual revert triggers** (in `useNavigationHandlers.ts`):
- User clicks "Stop" on an active seat route (`handleSeatNavigate` toggle-off)
- User dismisses the route overlay (`handleSeatRouteDismiss`)

The `revertWheelchairMode()` helper uses a functional updater on `setNavmeshMode` to guard against double-sends: only sends the Kit message if the current mode is `'wheelchair'`.

### Route cleanup on arrival/stop

When a seat route is stopped (arrival, manual stop, or dismiss), full cleanup ensures no stale routes survive a subsequent rebake:

1. **Kit side** (`extension.py`): `seatNavigate { action: 'stop' }` and successful seat teleport both call `self._svc.stop_route("player")` in addition to `stop_route("seat_nav")`. This removes any stale `player` route that the navigation orchestrator may have created.
2. **Web side**: All `navigationStateSet` messages that reset to `routeId: 'player'` include `endPos: null, endpointPath: null` to clear the orchestrator's stale endpoint. Without this, `_apply_state()` would recreate a `player` route with the old seat position, which `recalc_all_routes()` after a rebake would then redraw as a ghost path.
3. **Web side**: `navmeshRouteStop { routeId: 'player' }` is sent alongside `seatNavigate stop` in arrival handlers as a safety net.

### Cost category toggles (Avoid crowds / Avoid noise / Areas affect player movement)

The seat widget includes **"Avoid crowds"** and **"Avoid noise"** toggle buttons that control whether camera (crowd) or sound area costs are included in seat/NPC/exit pathfinding. The navigation hamburger menu has an **"Areas affect player movement"** toggle that controls whether all area costs affect point-and-click (player/default) routes. When OFF, those cost categories are ignored (treated as default 1.0); slider values remain stored and are used when re-activated. State: `avoidCrowds` / `avoidNoise` / `pointClickCostsActive` booleans. Frontend sends `navmeshCostCategoryToggle` event with `category: "crowd"|"sound"|"player"`; backend has `_crowd_costs_active` / `_sound_costs_active` / `_player_costs_active` flags on `NavMeshRouteService`. Cost gating is baked into lambdas at `_RouteInstance` creation: player routes gate on `_player_costs_active`, others on the per-category flags. See `.cursor/rules/topics/route-measurement.mdc` for full details.

## Route ID convention

- Seat routes always use `routeId = "seat_nav"` (fixed, not per-seat) -- only one seat route active at a time.
- Spot routes use the spot's `id` (e.g. `"wheelchair_ramp_01"`).
- The default player route uses `routeId = "player"`.

## Events summary

| Event | Direction | Payload | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `seatNavigate` | Web -> Kit | `{ section, row, seat, action? }` | Navigate to seat / stop |
| `seatNavigateResult` | Kit -> Web | `{ seatNumber, success, position?, error? }` | Seat found/not-found result |
| `seatTeleport` | Web -> Kit | `{ section, row, seat }` | Instant teleport to seat (sent via `onFadeOutComplete`) |
| `seatTeleportResult` | Kit -> Web | `{ seatNumber, success, position?, error? }` | Teleport result payload |
| `viewTransitionReady` | Kit -> Web | `{ result }` | Unified fade-in trigger (dispatched after `seatTeleportResult`) |
| `seatLayoutChange` | Web -> Kit | `{ variant }` | Switch seating variant |
| `seatLayoutChanged` | Kit -> Web | `{ variant, success, variants[] }` | Variant switch result |
| `navmeshRouteArrival` | Kit -> Web | `{ routeId, manualNearDestination? }` | Seat manual walk: endpoint **AABB** + `manualNearDestination`; other POIs: same AABB + path guard |
| `navmeshRouteError` | Kit -> Web | `{ routeId, error }` | Route calculation failure (generic, any route) |
| `playerFaceStadiumCenter` | Web -> Kit | `{}` | Seat celebration only -- bridge to `playerFaceWorldXZ` (not sent on teleport success) |
| `playerFaceWorldXZ` | Kit internal | `{ x, z }` | Smooth yaw toward world XZ point (orchestrator) |
| `younite.player.immediateViewAngles` | Kit internal | `{ yaw, pitch }` | Sync `PlayerInputController` after teleport sets camera yaw (see `poi-teleport.mdc`) |

